; Tutorial_5_Mark_Filter_and_Sort.inix -- choosing records, narrowing the list, ordering it.

[about]
Title=5 - Mark, Filter and Sort
Intro=Records marked one at a time and in runs, the list narrowed by a filter, and put in order by a column.
Setup=JobTrail is open in DbDo.
Homework=Filter your own table to one value, then sort what is left.

[step]

Say=One want: only the jobs still waiting, the newest first.
Key=
Hear=

[step]

Say=Alt plus Control plus D, D for DbDo, opens it or brings it forward.
Key=Alt+Control+D
Hear=DbDo
Hear=DbDo ready

[step]

Say=Control plus M, M for Mark, marks the record I am on, for a later command to act on.
Key=Control+M
Hear=Marked
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=Shift plus M asks about marks, changing nothing.
Key=Shift+M
Hear=(how many records are marked)
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=Control plus Shift plus M reverses it: Shift reverses.
Key=Control+Shift+M
Hear=Unmarked
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=Control plus F, F for Filter, shows only the records that match.
Key=Control+F
Hear=Filter Records dialog
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=I choose the status column, the value waiting, and press Enter. Shift plus F says the filter.
Key=Shift+F
Hear=status is waiting
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=Alt plus O, O for Order, sorts by a column; I choose the date added.
Key=Alt+O
Hear=Order Records dialog
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=Enter sorts. Alt plus Shift plus O reverses the order, newest first.
Key=Alt+Shift+O
Hear=(the newest waiting job)
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=A planned misstep: the filter stays until it is cleared, so a later search finds only waiting jobs. Control plus Shift plus F clears it.
Key=Control+Shift+F
Hear=No filter
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=What this walk taught. I name the command; the reader gives the key.
Key=
Hear=

[step]

Say=Mark, then unmark.
Key=
Hear=Control plus M
Hear=Control plus Shift plus M

[step]

Say=Filter, then clear it.
Key=
Hear=Control plus F
Hear=Control plus Shift plus F

[step]

Say=Order by a column.
Key=
Hear=Alt plus O
